{"step_index":298,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-08-25T21:01:44Z","content":"I have diagnosed and fixed the `FUNCTION_INVOCATION_FAILED` serverless crash!\n\n---\n\n### 🔍 Root Cause of the 500 Error\nOn Vercel's serverless Linux environment, the project code runs on a **read-only file system** (`/var/task`). When Vercel initialized the app, the asset helper functions attempted to create directories and copy fallback images, throwing an unhandled `OSError: Read-only file system` exception during startup.\n\n### 🛠️ Fix Applied\nI updated [`app.py`](file:///C:/Users/dell/.gemini/antigravity/brain/228fe0bc-0a77-489e-a1ba-57d617247457/app.py) with safe `try...except` blocks around all file copy and directory creation routines. If the environment is read-only (like Vercel), it safely skips local copies without crashing the app startup.\n\n---\n\n### 🚀 Push the Fix to GitHub & Vercel\n\nRun these commands in Command Prompt to push the fix and trigger automatic Vercel re-deployment:\n\n```cmd\ngit add .\n```\n\n```cmd\ngit commit -m \"fix: Protect asset copying against read-only serverless filesystem\"\n```\n\n```cmd\ngit push origin main\n```\n\nYour live Vercel deployment will re-deploy and launch your StreamWave application!"}
