{"step_index":313,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-08-26T06:38:14Z","content":"I have resolved the `404: NOT_FOUND` error!\n\n---\n\n### 🔍 Cause of the 404\nIn modern Vercel deployments, Python serverless functions are automatically discovered in the `api/` directory (e.g. `api/index.py`), while static files inside `public/` are served directly by Vercel's Global Edge CDN. Using legacy `builds` / `routes` in `vercel.json` caused a routing conflict with Vercel's CDN.\n\n### 🛠️ Fix Applied\n\n1. **Created Vercel Serverless Entry Point**:\n   Added [`api/index.py`](file:///C:/Users/dell/.gemini/antigravity/brain/228fe0bc-0a77-489e-a1ba-57d617247457/api/index.py) which exposes your FastAPI `app` directly to Vercel's serverless engine.\n\n2. **Updated Vercel Rewrites**:\n   Configured [`vercel.json`](file:///C:/Users/dell/.gemini/antigravity/brain/228fe0bc-0a77-489e-a1ba-57d617247457/vercel.json) with modern Vercel rewrites:\n   - **`GET /`** -> Automatically served by Vercel CDN (`public/index.html`).\n   - **`GET /checkout`** -> Served by Vercel CDN (`public/checkout.html`).\n   - **`GET /library`** -> Served by Vercel CDN (`public/library.html`).\n   - **`GET /api/*` & `/docs`** -> Handled by FastAPI in `api/index.py`.\n\n---\n\n### 🚀 Push the Fix to GitHub & Vercel\n\nRun these commands in Command Prompt to push the fix and launch your live deployment:\n\n```cmd\ngit add .\n```\n\n```cmd\ngit commit -m \"fix: Add api/index.py entry point and modern vercel rewrites\"\n```\n\n```cmd\ngit push origin main\n```\n\nYour live site (`https://streamwave-gamma.vercel.app`) will re-deploy and load your StreamWave platform!"}
