{"step_index":317,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-08-26T06:58:25Z","content":"I have resolved the `Not Found` error on the payment simulation endpoint!\n\n---\n\n### 🔍 Root Cause\nWhen Vercel delegating requests from `/api/demo-payment` to the Python serverless function `api/index.py`, Vercel stripped the `/api` prefix in its serverless invocation context (passing `/demo-payment` to FastAPI). Because FastAPI only looked for `@app.post(\"/api/demo-payment\")`, FastAPI returned `404 Not Found`.\n\n### 🛠️ Fix Applied\nI updated [`app.py`](file:///C:/Users/dell/.gemini/antigravity/brain/228fe0bc-0a77-489e-a1ba-57d617247457/app.py) to add **dual route path aliases** across all endpoints:\n- `@app.post(\"/api/demo-payment\")` **AND** `@app.post(\"/demo-payment\")`\n- `@app.get(\"/api/session\")` **AND** `@app.get(\"/session\")`\n- `@app.get(\"/api/media\")` **AND** `@app.get(\"/media\")`\n- `@app.post(\"/api/play-events\")` **AND** `@app.post(\"/play-events\")`\n\nNow, whether Vercel passes `/api/demo-payment` or `/demo-payment`, FastAPI will match with 200 OK and issue the signed session cookie!\n\n---\n\n### 🚀 Push the Fix to GitHub & Vercel\n\nRun these commands in Command Prompt to push the fix and update your live Vercel deployment:\n\n```cmd\ngit add .\n```\n\n```cmd\ngit commit -m \"fix: Add dual route path aliases (/api/endpoint & /endpoint) for Vercel rewrite compatibility\"\n```\n\n```cmd\ngit push origin main\n```\n\nOnce pushed, Vercel will re-deploy and your checkout button will approve payments and redirect to the member library!"}
